{"term":"pochwa","lang":"pl","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"organs","subcategory":"vagina","concept":"vagina","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"clinical","crude":5,"technical":95,"recognition_pct_current":90,"recognition_pct_peak":90,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"The standard clinical Polish term for the vagina; the internal muscular canal extending from the cervix to the vulval opening.","english_term":"vagina","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"The word also means 'scabbard' or 'sheath' in general Polish, sharing etymology with Latin 'vagina' (scabbard); both meanings are widely known; taught in school biology and used throughout medical and public health communication."}
{"term":"srom","lang":"pl","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"organs","subcategory":"vulva","concept":"vulva","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"clinical","crude":5,"technical":95,"recognition_pct_current":72,"recognition_pct_peak":72,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"The clinical Polish term for the vulva; the collective external female genitalia including the labia, clitoris, and vaginal opening.","english_term":"vulva","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"Less widely recognized by lay speakers than 'pochwa'; frequently confused with 'vagina' in non-medical usage; the root 'srom-' appears in compound anatomical terms ('wargi sromowe', 'wzgórek sromowy'); old Slavic origin."}
{"term":"wargi sromowe","lang":"pl","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"organs","subcategory":"labia","concept":"labia","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"clinical","crude":5,"technical":90,"recognition_pct_current":80,"recognition_pct_peak":80,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"The clinical Polish term for the labia; literally 'vulvar lips', referring collectively to the labial folds of the female external genitalia.","english_term":"labia","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"The adjective 'sromowe' derives from 'srom' (vulva); used in medical education, gynaecological consultations, and public health contexts; without a qualifier ('większe'/'mniejsze') refers generically to both sets of labia."}
{"term":"wargi sromowe większe","lang":"pl","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"organs","subcategory":"labia_majora","concept":"labia_majora","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"clinical","crude":5,"technical":95,"recognition_pct_current":62,"recognition_pct_peak":62,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"The clinical Polish term for the labia majora; the outer, larger folds of skin forming the outer boundary of the vulva.","english_term":"labia majora","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"Literally 'larger vulvar lips'; recognized primarily by those with medical or anatomical education; standard in gynaecological and anatomy texts."}
